ions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it did not qualify.) After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14973, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014i117Qs23cYS6ShvuzFEWD", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14973, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014i117Qs23cYS6ShvuzFEWD", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18147, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Rollback version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was newer, but it was only healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **After the rollback:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service passes health checks, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open. It records what failed, why I picked v2.3.0, the results after the rollback, and a follow-up to find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01XyfAkA45PLwQ7Jd8xp6sn1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016VEGFRqEdBVr4wZXBkghhk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01LLZGYKYVMvG5yLHr5pbU7d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Hnj6XemRcJapuXivodhTkC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013Ji9qF228BSQVEm6hqu33u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014i117Qs23cYS6ShvuzFEWD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed to production, the service failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. We rolled it back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it did not qualify.) After the rollback, all regions run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Rollback version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was newer, but it was only healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **After the rollback:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service passes health checks, and the error rate is 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open. It records what failed, why I picked v2.3.0, the results after the rollback, and a follow-up to find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}